    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The BODMAS rule establishes the operational precedence: Brackets, Orders, Division, Multiplication, Addition, Subtraction.",
        "Speed calculations in RRB exams depend heavily on percentage conversion tricks and ratio-based simplification.",
        "Approximation strategies help save critical time when options allow estimated values.",
        "Algebraic identity shortcuts and surd simplification streamline complex numerical expressions."
      ],
      "id": "2hokzmj"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cz8xslk",
      "content": "Simplification is one of the highest return topics in RRB mathematics because it directly affects speed. Many arithmetic questions become manageable only when calculations are performed efficiently."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tn8tomk",
      "content": "Students who master simplification:"
    },
    {
      "id": "6icvhqq",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Attempt more questions</li><li>Save time for difficult problems</li><li>Reduce calculation errors</li><li>Gain confidence during the exam</li></ul>",
        "Attempt more questions",
        "Save time for difficult problems",
        "Reduce calculation errors",
        "Gain confidence during the exam"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bz0myom",
      "content": "Simplification is not about difficult mathematics — it is about smart mathematics."
    },
    {
      "id": "drz2lm2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "The BODMAS Rule – The Golden Principle"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dodi6oj",
      "content": "Whenever an expression contains multiple operations, they must be solved in the correct order:"
    },
    {
      "id": "2diom9c",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Brackets → Orders (powers/roots) → Division → Multiplication → Addition → Subtraction."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5jj5q9o",
      "content": "Important Note:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2fbe9h9",
      "content": "Division and multiplication are performed from left to right. The same rule applies to addition and subtraction."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ggz1f2k",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vqw9ucc",
      "content": "20 – 6 ÷ 3 × 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hdpgt4r",
      "content": "Step 1: Division → 6 ÷ 3 = 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "y1qbrmy",
      "content": "Step 2: Multiplication → 2 × 2 = 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p5va6ib",
      "content": "Step 3: Subtraction → 20 – 4 = 16"
    },
    {
      "id": "ug11eyr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Types of Brackets"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ep8x0nd",
      "content": "When multiple brackets appear, solve them in this order:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fuys5bc",
      "content": "Vinculum (—) → Parentheses ( ) → Curly braces { } → Square brackets [ ] Always simplify inner brackets first before moving outward."
    },
    {
      "id": "dk65o0w",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Fraction Simplification"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mfntw6y",
      "content": "Fractions should always be reduced before multiplication whenever possible. Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ht3vfca",
      "content": "(24 × 15) / 6"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l8uwb2f",
      "content": "Cancel first:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "o7vihz5",
      "content": "24 ÷ 6 = 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yzcylfm",
      "content": "Now multiply:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "wrzo6a7",
      "content": "4 × 15 = 60"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0sofc3o",
      "content": "This saves time and prevents large-number multiplication."
    },
    {
      "id": "nhigrp6",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "<strong>Decimal Simplification Trick </strong>Convert decimals into fractions when helpful. Example:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "u4wlbtf",
      "content": "0.25 × 64"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "zp2g4os",
      "content": "0.25 = 1/4"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "09gv9ug",
      "content": "64 ÷ 4 = 16"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "axydldw",
      "content": "Answer = 16."
    },
    {
      "id": "0qkh3d4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Percentage Conversion Trick"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tijs2tf",
      "content": "Convert percentages into fractions for faster solving. 125% = 5/4"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "nnod7ub",
      "content": "150% = 3/2"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "n9htk99",
      "content": "12.5% = 1/8"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k10imo3",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "uw3m6d6",
      "content": "150% of 48"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "8s58031",
      "content": "= (3/2) × 48"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "gyct3i2",
      "content": "= 72"
    },
    {
      "id": "rerl35b",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Ratio-Based Simplification"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a7vuqjo",
      "content": "Expressions involving ratios can often be simplified through cancellation. Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "qmd03ue",
      "content": "(48 × 25) ÷ 16"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "4ipg006",
      "content": "48 ÷ 16 = 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7hz1cxb",
      "content": "3 × 25 = 75."
    },
    {
      "id": "8gzouhi",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Multiplication Tricks for Speed"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rl7fk3t",
      "content": "Multiply by 5 → multiply by 10 and divide by 2. Multiply by 25 → multiply by 100 and divide by 4."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1lonb52",
      "content": "Multiply by 125 → multiply by 1000 and divide by 8. Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "hn48pir",
      "content": "64 × 125"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "dw2tsmp",
      "content": "= 64000 ÷ 8"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ia08jtk",
      "content": "= 8000."
    },
    {
      "id": "y4fdu9s",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Approximation Strategy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wdqdwg9",
      "content": "Approximation is extremely useful when answer options are far apart. Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "neuq5uk",
      "content": "498 × 19"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "n9hfcq0",
      "content": "=500 × 20"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dw4gx73",
      "content": "= 10000."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gzl8j04",
      "content": "Use approximation only when precision is unnecessary."
    },
    {
      "id": "96xo0bb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Surd Simplification"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b2bwjlj",
      "content": "Break the number into perfect square factors."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mlsm30t",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "fy83oon",
      "content": "√98"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "51lc10i",
      "content": "= √(49 × 2)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "me04pvs",
      "content": "= 7√2."
    },
    {
      "id": "6o7atr8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Algebraic Identity Shortcuts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "61hqu41",
      "content": "(a + b)² = a² + b² + 2ab (a – b)² = a² + b² – 2ab (a + b)(a – b) = a² – b² Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "z4mcxgt",
      "content": "102²"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "d6skbwo",
      "content": "= (100 + 2)²"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j3z7gqm",
      "content": "= 10000 + 4 + 400"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ls15aix",
      "content": "= 10404."
    },
    {
      "id": "4l77ixq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Exam-Level Tricks Summary"
    },
    {
      "id": "rmny118",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Cancel early.</li><li>Convert percentages into fractions.</li><li>Look for powers of 10.</li><li>Approximate when possible.</li><li>Apply identities for large numbers.</li></ul>",
        "Cancel early.",
        "Convert percentages into fractions.",
        "Look for powers of 10.",
        "Approximate when possible.",
        "Apply identities for large numbers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dn2oq03",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Solved Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zmvnhms",
      "content": "Example 1:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "eymnpzw",
      "content": "Evaluate: 48 ÷ 4 × 5 + 6"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lsz78ew",
      "content": "Step 1: Division → 48 ÷ 4 = 12"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0a50esk",
      "content": "Step 2: Multiplication → 12 × 5 = 60"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uavwb5l",
      "content": "Step 3: Addition → 60 + 6 = 66."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "2rqm396",
      "content": "Final Answer: 66"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i7znqfh",
      "content": "Example 2:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bw8gbge",
      "content": "Simplify: (75 × 16) ÷ 25 Cancel first:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "cro2f82",
      "content": "75 ÷ 25 = 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "adhj6xj",
      "content": "Now multiply:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gv1t7z3",
      "content": "3 × 16 = 48."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "tnh2xxz",
      "content": "Final Answer: 48"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yphco2x",
      "content": "Example 3:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m6y7ld5",
      "content": "Find the value of √144 + 12²."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "li08dlo",
      "content": "√144 = 12"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "qanlawg",
      "content": "12² = 144"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fm9j4zl",
      "content": "Total = 12 + 144 = 156."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i4lwehq",
      "content": "Final Answer: 156."
    },
    {
      "id": "abipshl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Practice Questions with VERY DETAILED Solutions"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fxa0x6l",
      "content": "Question 1:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dztuj6v",
      "content": "Evaluate: 36 + 24 ÷ 6 × 5."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6cqy7uk",
      "content": "Step 1: Apply BODMAS."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "2x2zh1g",
      "content": "24 ÷ 6 = 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tfg17ba",
      "content": "Step 2: Multiply."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "so115n9",
      "content": "4 × 5 = 20"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2yri2lc",
      "content": "Step 3: Add."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "oyn7v0w",
      "content": "36 + 20 = 56"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xkmjqou",
      "content": "Final Answer: 56."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lv21m75",
      "content": "Question 2: Simplify: (64 × 25) ÷ 8."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "op88kxv",
      "content": "Step 1: Cancel before multiplying. 64 ÷ 8 = 8"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3jx7f8q",
      "content": "Step 2: Multiply."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "iibat80",
      "content": "8 × 25 = 200"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9z6r08i",
      "content": "Final Answer: 200."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fqjlgtg",
      "content": "Question 3: Find 12.5% of 96."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cz237bx",
      "content": "Step 1: Convert percentage into fraction. 12.5% = 1/8"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mvzkk69",
      "content": "Step 2: Divide."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "tigigo3",
      "content": "96 ÷ 8 = 12"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yfp7m0d",
      "content": "Final Answer: 12."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jva7hci",
      "content": "Question 4:Evaluate: 102 × 98."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Strictly evaluate operations following BODMAS priority to avoid common calculation traps.",
        "Memorize standard fraction-to-percentage conversions for immediate substitution during exams.",
        "Apply algebraic shortcut identities directly to large numerical expressions for fast solving."
      ],
      "id": "s4pdjer"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k9sr5ec",
      "content": "Step 1: Use identity (a+b)(a-b) = a² – b². Let a = 100, b = 2."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3xazr6p",
      "content": "Step 2:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "dlsyjlv",
      "content": "100² – 2²"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "b0qmd7t",
      "content": "= 10000 – 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "8kx2dbu",
      "content": "= 9996"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "upgxfgc",
      "content": "Final Answer: 9996."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o2ujctw",
      "content": "Question 5:Approximate 497 × 21. Step 1: Round the numbers."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "wpipxnf",
      "content": "497≈ 500"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "3rs6qx1",
      "content": "21 ≈ 20"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m2m3zvn",
      "content": "Step 2: Multiply."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "jkbcxf4",
      "content": "500 × 20 = 10000"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8c3u3xi",
      "content": "Final Answer: Approximately 10,000. Question 6: Simplify √50 + √18."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lwg5by7",
      "content": "Step 1: Break into perfect squares."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "n86ih28",
      "content": "√50 = √(25×2) = 5√2"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "sv3ev4v",
      "content": "√18 = √(9×2) = 3√2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zd932bu",
      "content": "Step 2: Add like surds. 5√2"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "0pbmgeh",
      "content": "+ 3√2 = 8√2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7bao852",
      "content": "Final Answer: 8√2."
    },
    {
      "id": "zn4pcjd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Final Author Insight"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jo95brz",
      "content": "Simplification is not just a topic — it is a competitive advantage."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5rguja6",
      "content": "Students who develop fast calculation instincts conserve mental energy for difficult questions and maintain accuracy under time pressure.Master this chapter, and you will notice a visible jump in your solving speed across the entire mathematics section."
    }
  ],
